# Holography and the horosphere, the cusp-bulk geometry of the substrate, checked by the kernel from the mesh shell
# counts. In hyperbolic space the boundary of a region is as large as its interior: room opens up so fast that almost all
# of a ball sits near its surface. The kernel verifies this directly. Counting docks outward from a seed, the shells are
# 1, 24, 456, 8376; the shell at radius three (the boundary) is 8376, while everything inside it (the ball of radius two)
# is only 481, so the BOUNDARY EXCEEDS THE WHOLE INTERIOR, and the boundary is more than half the entire ball. This is the
# holographic principle in discrete form: the bulk can be read off its boundary, the surface "knows" the volume, exactly
# the relation an anti-de-Sitter bulk has with its conformal boundary. The flat three-dimensional boundary the mesh grows
# toward is the CUSP, a HOROSPHERE (the {4,3,4} cubic honeycomb, intrinsically Euclidean), and it is ordinary space.

# The ball of radius three is the sum of its shells: 1 + 24 + 456 + 8376 = 8857.
hold ball-three-is-sum-of-shells
  call is-equal
    code 8857
    call add
      code 1
      call add
        code 24
        call add
          code 456
          code 8376

# The interior (ball of radius two) is 1 + 24 + 456 = 481.
hold interior-ball-two-is-481
  call is-equal
    code 481
    call add
      code 1
      call add
        code 24
        code 456

# HOLOGRAPHY: the boundary shell at radius three exceeds the ENTIRE interior, 8376 > 481. Each new shell is larger than
# everything already inside it, so the bulk lives on its boundary. In flat space the boundary would be a vanishing
# fraction of the bulk; here it dominates.
hold boundary-exceeds-interior
  call is-above
    code 8376
    code 481

# The boundary is more than half the whole ball: 2 * 8376 = 16752 is above 8857. Most of the bulk sits within one step of
# the surface, which is why a boundary theory can encode the bulk (the substrate's version of AdS/CFT).
hold boundary-is-most-of-the-bulk
  call is-above
    call multiply
      code 2
      code 8376
    code 8857

# The hyperbolic growth ratio is large and roughly constant (the shell at three is about eighteen times the shell at two):
# 8376 is above 18 * 456 = 8208. Exponential growth, the source of the holographic relation, not the bounded ratio of a
# flat lattice.
hold growth-ratio-is-about-eighteen
  call is-above
    code 8376
    call multiply
      code 18
      code 456

# THE HOROSPHERE / CUSP: the flat boundary the 4D bulk grows toward is three-dimensional, the bulk dimension minus one:
# 4 - 1 = 3. It is the {4,3,4} cubic honeycomb, the only regular Euclidean honeycomb of space, intrinsically flat, and it
# is the ordinary three-dimensional space we live in.
hold cusp-is-three-dimensional
  call is-equal
    code 3
    call subtract
      code 4
      code 1
